[0.508, "o", "\u001b[90m│\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[32m◆\u001b[39m  Giant Squid Claude-to-Codex bridge is listening\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  base URL:  http://127.0.0.1:8765\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  backend:   codex exec\r\n  tier:     strong\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  config:   model_reasoning_effort=\"high\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  official:  no - compatibility bridge only\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "╭─ Giant Squid :: Claude-shaped local bridge ────────────────────────────────╮\r\n│ Base URL  http://127.0.0.1:8765                                            │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "│ Auth      generated per run                                                │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "│ Tier      strong                                                           │\r\n│ Backend   codex exec                                                       │\r\n│ Aliases   request model passes through                                     │\r\n│ Use now   client launched with Anthropic env injected                      │\r\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "│ Routes    GET /health  POST /v1/messages  POST /v1/messages/count_tokens │\r\n│ Boundary  unofficial compatibility layer; not Claude Code auth            │\r\n╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\nLaunching: claude -p In two sentences: what does 'port daddy' the port manager do for multi-agent development?\r\n"]
[34.414, "o", "Port Daddy gives every agent/service a stable semantic identity and deterministic port, so parallel agents can run local dev servers without trampling each other. It also coordinates sessions, file claims, notes, locks, salvage, and handoff evidence so multi-agent work stays visible and recoverable.\r\n"]
